STARTER Explain
===============

1. OVERVIEW
===========

starter-explain is a long-running daemon that attaches to starter-core's
remote debug server (GDBus over TCP), tracks I/O state grouped into
contexts defined in an XML configuration, and on relevant I/O changes
builds a prompt for an external LLM, converts the reply to speech via an
external TTS service, and plays the audio.

The LLM, optional RAG index, and TTS server are external.  This repository
ships the daemon, a commented demo configuration, and the Texinfo manual.

2. PREREQUISITES
================

* GLib / GObject / GIO (libglib2.0-dev)
* libxml2 (libxml2-dev)
* json-glib (libjson-glib-dev)
* libsoup 3.x or 2.4 >= 2.58
* Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
* Optional: texinfo (to build the manual)

3. BUILDING
===========

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

Documentation (Info):

    $ make -C doc

4. USAGE
========

See the commented example and the manual:

    examples/demo.stex.xml
    info starter-explain   # after make install / make -C doc

    $ starter-explain --config=examples/demo.stex.xml
    $ starter-explain --config=FILE --core=HOST:PORT --dry-run

Enable debug logs with:

    $ G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=all starter-explain --config=FILE

